# PR #450 Review

## Findings

### MUST-FIX

1. "'`tests/triage-cli.test.ts:886`
   The new integration test is annotated as `// AC: @interactive-triage ac-1, ac-2`, but the AC-2 assertion is incomplete. AC-2 is specifically about what the export captures "when the export is generated" (full decision chain with attribution and timestamps). This test only checks the exported context for item/action/override reasoning, then validates attribution/timestamps through `triage list` JSON instead. That can pass even if `triage export --format context` omits required attribution/timestamp fields.

## AC / Spec Coverage Check

- PR body does not include an exact `Task: @...` trailer, but it does include `@implement-interactive-triage-system` / `@interactive-triage`, so I used those refs for review.
- `kspec task get @implement-interactive-triage-system`: linked spec is `@interactive-triage` with ACs `ac-1` and `ac-2`.
- `kspec item get @interactive-triage --json`: `inherited_traits` is empty, so there are no trait ACs to cover for this spec.
- `rg "// AC: @interactive-triage" ...`: annotations exist for both `ac-1` and `ac-2`, but `ac-2` coverage is overstated for export semantics (see finding above).

## Validation / Test Runs

- `kspec validate`: schema/references pass; no `@interactive-triage` trait-coverage warning surfaced. Command exits non-zero due pre-existing project-wide alignment/completeness warnings.
- `pnpm vitest tests/triage-cli.test.ts tests/triage-parser.test.ts`: 72/72 passing.
EOF

